{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/836657-request-espionage-fiction","id":836657,"title":"Request - Espionage Fiction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-24T13:50:24-08:00","id":836657,"title":"Request - Espionage Fiction","content":"The Demon: The Descent Core book comes with a lot of great recommendations for espionage fiction and media, however, John le Carr\u00e9's work, while amazing and rightfully recommended in the fiction section of Demon, isn't in the same modern pacing of a lot of current espionage fiction. Demon pointed me towards the TV series Person of Interest, and I have totally fallen in love with that show because of it. I am looking for something similar but in novel form.<br /> <br /> Is there any similar or more modern espionage fiction that anyone could recommend? Bonus points if its close to the themes Demon or Person of Interest espouse, like information, Big Brother type surveillance and conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for any suggestions!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T15:50:08-08:00","id":836716,"title":"","content":"We've <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15892-shows-to-watch-for-inspiration\">done</a> a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/682753-can-anyone-recommend-anymore-inspirational-for-demon-the-decent\">few</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/449626-a-game-in-istanbul-looking-for-material\">threads</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/403903-spycraft-for-kids\">on</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24751-book-inspirations\">this</a>, but:<br /> <br /> <u>Zeros</u> by Chuck Wendig<br /> <br /> the <u>For Queen or Country</u> series by Greg Rucka, which has both novels and graphic novels<br /> <br /> <u>Little Brother</u> by Cory Doctrow<br /> <br /> Most of the stuff written by Charles Cummings.<br /> <br /> <u>Boku ga Inai Machi</u> if you enjoy anime.<br /> <br /> <u>The Worricker Trilogy</u> and <u>Deutschland 83 </u>are worth watching.<br /> <br /> I can't recommend <u>Black Mirror</u> enough, though that's less espionage and more &quot;Sweet Baby Machine-Jesus, what did I just watch?&quot; mind screw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-24-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T16:11:05-08:00","id":836725,"title":"","content":"Only sort of Espionage, but I recommend Daemon and Freedom<sup>TM </sup>by Daniel Suarez. More investigative techno-thriller than real espionage, but it has similar feels to Person of interest in a lot of ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T14:11:28-08:00","id":837210,"title":"","content":"Awesome suggestions! Thanks both of you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:19:47-08:00","id":844249,"title":"","content":"While a little more archaic than what you want, Tim Power's &quot;Declare&quot; is a Cold War spy novel about a British agent brought back in to clean up a djinn-related mess. It's incredible, and really fun Dark Eras inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T22:22:43-08:00","id":844350,"title":"","content":"Here's one I haven't seen tossed in the mix that is excellent: the <u>Sigma Force</u> series by James Rollins. It's not traditional spy literature since it focuses on the scientists and covert forces of DARPA, but there is a lot of study of scientific phenomenon crossed over with various religious overtones. I could almost describe it as James Bond meets Indiana Jones and Alan Grant. And there are some awesome ideas for Angels and Infrastrucutre in these novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"J